  "question": {
    "text": "A differentiable function <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> satisfies <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></math>, then (where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;represents derivative of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math>)",
