  "solution": {
    "text": "Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></math><br />Now,&nbsp;<math><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> &amp; <math><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />As <math><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is differentiable, so by Rolle&rsquo;s theorem,<br /><math> <mrow> <msup> <mi>g</mi> <mo>&#8242;</mo> </msup> <mfenced> <mi>c</mi> </mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow> </math> for some <math><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0,1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />i.e. <math> <mrow> <msup> <mi>f</mi> <mo>&#8242;</mo> </msup> <mfenced> <mi>c</mi> </mfenced><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow> </math><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8658;</mo><msup> <mi>f</mi> <mo>&#8242;</mo> </msup> <mfenced> <mi>c</mi> </mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>c</mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mtext>for</mtext><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mtext>some</mtext><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"> <mrow> <mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow> </mfenced></mrow> </math>",
